    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 16 with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.26), who is our clear primary target today. Facing Dobbins, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite dynamic platoon matchup (+14%) and the leadoff spot (+10%), offering the highest sprint-speed-to-production upside in our lineup. **Yordan Alvarez** (65.52) remains an essential start despite the matchup against Bryan Woo; his elite xwOBA (0.465) and favorable order placement make him a pillar of our offensive floor. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (62.27) and **Kyle Schwarber** (60.40) provide the requisite power-hitting stability, with **Kyle Schwarber**\u2019s leadoff positioning mitigating the risk posed by Kremer.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin** (48.55), who narrowly missed the cutoff. While **Caleb Durbin**\u2019s profile is enhanced by his elite situational speed and a favorable 100% SB delivery environment against Bachar, he failed to crack the starting nine due to superior efficiency from our mid-order anchors like **Colt Keith** (50.92) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.56). Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Gary Sanchez** (41.24); his proximity to our 40.0 floor is concerning given he is facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm in Skubal. While we prioritize **Gary Sanchez** for his platoon edge, he is on high alert for mid-game substitution should his efficiency trend downward.\n\nManagement is keeping a close eye on the overall ledger to ensure we do not exceed game caps, particularly with **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (52.89) and **Carson Benge** (53.48) providing reliable, if unspectacular, production in the middle of our order. The current configuration maximizes our SB potential\u2014critical for our 5x5 Roto standing\u2014without sacrificing the core R/RBI output required to keep pace in the standings. No major weather alerts are currently threatening play, meaning we expect full participation from our starters as we look to capitalize on the weak pitching matchups for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Junior Caminero**.",
